the united states economy is officially  in a recession we just got the brand new  gdp data from q2 and it was negative  that is two consecutive quarters of  negative gdp growth which meets the  technical definition of a recession now  many of you have probably heard the  white house and other people in  positions of power and influence start  to gaslight the american people on what  actually defines a recession regardless  of what they say professional market  participants and sophisticated investors  all agree two consecutive quarters of  negative gdp growth means that we are in  a recession now this is absolutely  incredible because economists and market  forecasters they actually were  predicting positive gdp growth it's  understandable when they make a mistake  and they don't actually nail it and  they're off by a few percentage points  but to think that it's going to be  positive and it ends up being negative  that's outright asinine now of course we  also know that the federal reserve has  made two major mistakes over the last 12  months  first they were conducting quantitative  easing and holding interest rates  artificially low when inflation was  already over seven percent last year  now the federal reserve has been hiking  interest rates as we headed into a  recession in both scenarios the federal  reserve has been behind the curve  now i'm not one of the conspiracy  theorists i don't think that there's  some master plan for a controlled  demolition of the american economy i  actually think that the federal reserve  economists and market forecasters  they're trying to do the right thing  it's more of a hanlen's razor situation  don't assign malice to something that  can simply be explained by ignorance but  that doesn't change the fact that we  have high inflation in america it's at a  40-year high and now we're also in a  recession hello stagflation in these  scenarios it is a lose-lose if the fed  does not act we will continue to have  persistently high inflation if the fed  destroys demand as they've outlined as  their goal we will head deeper and  deeper into a recession  ultimately the federal reserve is going  to have to capitulate in one direction  or the other my guess is that the  federal reserve will capitulate they  will have to mitigate the recession and  just let people live with high inflation  that's not a great solution but it's the  best of the worst possible solutions  ultimately the u.s economy is in a very  perplexing and unique situation  we still have pretty strong employment  and consumer spending has not fallen but  we see gdp contracting we see high  inflation and we also see the federal  reserve is worried about where we could  go from here ultimately you have to  simply look at the data you have to be  willing to admit the problems and the  potential solutions we're in a recession  regardless of what anyone says and we  have high inflation and is likely higher  than the official numbers  lose lose situation what you at home  have to do is you have to make sure you  have a strong balance sheet you have to  optimize your cash flow and you simply  have to try to survive the next six to  12 months get to the other side and you  earn the right to thrive during the next  bull run  but until then  get ready for a bumpy ride
 

